1
00:00:00,335 --> 00:00:05,215
Right now my leg is hanging through the
ceiling over a hundred dead people, and my

2
00:00:05,235 --> 00:00:07,355
best friend is walking right under it.

3
00:00:07,375 --> 00:00:09,685
The edge of the hole is
cutting into my thigh.

4
00:00:09,835 --> 00:00:11,885
My right boot is caught
on something sharp.

5
00:00:11,975 --> 00:00:15,425
Every time I try to move, a little
more white dust falls past my foot.

6
00:00:15,580 --> 00:00:19,670
A piece the size of my thumbnail
lands on the fountain rim.

7
00:00:19,700 --> 00:00:22,410
The little tick carries
through the whole court.

8
00:00:22,500 --> 00:00:24,950
Under my leg, somebody starts moving.

9
00:00:25,284 --> 00:00:27,484
There are faces turned up toward me.

10
00:00:27,504 --> 00:00:31,774
A woman with one earring. A man
still holding a shopping bag.

11
00:00:31,804 --> 00:00:36,224
The cleaner who used to leave a yellow
cone outside the bathrooms, even when the

12
00:00:36,244 --> 00:00:37,334
floor was dry.

13
00:00:37,424 --> 00:00:38,324
And Marcus.

14
00:00:38,344 --> 00:00:42,704
He comes around the fountain in his guard
uniform, stops at a gate, and shakes it

15
00:00:42,724 --> 00:00:43,524
twice.

16
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:44,544
Same as always.

17
00:00:44,603 --> 00:00:49,173
The empty clip on his chest
catches the emergency light.

18
00:00:49,703 --> 00:00:51,373
His radio is in my pocket.

19
00:00:51,423 --> 00:00:54,333
I took the battery out
before we climbed up here.

20
00:00:54,723 --> 00:00:56,204
At least I got one thing right.

21
00:00:56,224 --> 00:00:59,714
Above me, Theo is lying
flat on a metal beam.

22
00:00:59,844 --> 00:01:01,814
He's got both hands around my wrist.

23
00:01:01,924 --> 00:01:06,084
His trainers are braced against a pipe,
and he's pulling hard enough that his whole

24
00:01:06,104 --> 00:01:07,104
face shakes.

25
00:01:07,284 --> 00:01:08,314
He looks at my boot.

26
00:01:08,564 --> 00:01:10,144
Then he looks at the ceiling around it.

27
00:01:10,164 --> 00:01:11,159
Danny,

28
00:01:11,179 --> 00:01:12,030
he says.

29
00:01:12,050 --> 00:01:13,050
Stop moving.

30
00:01:13,285 --> 00:01:14,285
I stop.

31
00:01:14,645 --> 00:01:16,155
Another corner breaks off anyway.

32
00:01:16,405 --> 00:01:20,735
The only person who can pull me out is
a kid I nearly threw out of my store.

33
00:01:21,185 --> 00:01:22,185
Let me back up.

34
00:01:26,997 --> 00:01:31,177
The woman on the radio asked who was
in my daughter's window, and I gave her

35
00:01:31,197 --> 00:01:31,977
nothing.

36
00:01:31,997 --> 00:01:33,507
I took my thumb off the button.

37
00:01:34,057 --> 00:01:37,347
For six years, answering
that radio had been my job.

38
00:01:37,557 --> 00:01:41,637
A call came in, I said my name, and whoever
was on the other end knew somebody was

39
00:01:41,657 --> 00:01:42,362
coming.

40
00:01:42,382 --> 00:01:45,152
Now I had to remind myself
that I could leave it alone.

41
00:01:45,382 --> 00:01:46,932
My phone was in my other hand.

42
00:01:47,062 --> 00:01:48,042
No service.

43
00:01:48,062 --> 00:01:51,752
My mom's last message was still
there, telling me the door was locked.

44
00:01:51,922 --> 00:01:53,692
I read it again while the woman waited.

45
00:01:53,862 --> 00:01:58,092
I wanted somebody to talk to badly enough
that I was afraid of what I might say.

46
00:01:58,249 --> 00:02:01,839
Across the highway, the
tenth-floor window stayed dark.

47
00:02:02,729 --> 00:02:04,779
Lily had already blinked three times.

48
00:02:05,309 --> 00:02:06,309
I'd answered.

49
00:02:06,749 --> 00:02:07,959
Our goodnight was over.

50
00:02:09,209 --> 00:02:12,609
The woman waited long enough that I could
hear her breathing through the little

51
00:02:12,629 --> 00:02:13,426
speaker.

52
00:02:13,446 --> 00:02:14,252
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Danny?

53
00:02:14,272 --> 00:02:18,522
I turned the volume down and
held the radio against my ear.

54
00:02:18,703 --> 00:02:19,703
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] You still there?

55
00:02:19,842 --> 00:02:24,812
I could see a faint light moving behind
the department store's rooftop door.

56
00:02:24,922 --> 00:02:26,792
When I looked again, it was gone.

57
00:02:26,902 --> 00:02:27,902
I pressed the button.

58
00:02:28,002 --> 00:02:29,312
How did you get inside?

59
00:02:29,382 --> 00:02:30,382
A little laugh.

60
00:02:30,595 --> 00:02:32,925
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] That's
a fairly rude first question.

61
00:02:33,310 --> 00:02:34,480
You asked me one.

62
00:02:34,765 --> 00:02:35,765
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Fair enough.

63
00:02:36,065 --> 00:02:36,765
Vera.

64
00:02:36,785 --> 00:02:37,245
There.

65
00:02:37,265 --> 00:02:38,355
Now you have a name.

66
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:39,540
I waited.

67
00:02:39,624 --> 00:02:41,254
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] I
was trying on a coat.

68
00:02:41,624 --> 00:02:42,584
Department store.

69
00:02:42,604 --> 00:02:43,544
Second floor.

70
00:02:43,564 --> 00:02:45,974
Sat down in the fitting
room and fell asleep.

71
00:02:46,164 --> 00:02:48,794
By the time I woke up,
they'd locked the place.

72
00:02:49,047 --> 00:02:52,317
The store had closed at nine.

73
00:02:52,487 --> 00:02:56,387
At midnight, I'd checked the staff
corridor behind those fitting rooms.

74
00:02:56,407 --> 00:02:57,407
I'd heard nothing.

75
00:02:57,527 --> 00:02:58,857
What coat?

76
00:02:59,087 --> 00:02:59,848
I asked.

77
00:02:59,868 --> 00:03:00,593
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] What?

78
00:03:00,613 --> 00:03:02,043
The one you were trying on.

79
00:03:02,261 --> 00:03:06,231
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Danny, there
are people eating people downstairs.

80
00:03:06,681 --> 00:03:09,471
I think we've moved
beyond the returns policy.

81
00:03:09,881 --> 00:03:12,551
She sounded almost amused.

82
00:03:12,801 --> 00:03:14,551
Then her voice changed a little.

83
00:03:14,758 --> 00:03:16,788
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] There's
a girl up here with me.

84
00:03:16,998 --> 00:03:17,998
She's hungry.

85
00:03:18,058 --> 00:03:19,548
Have you got anything we could eat?

86
00:03:19,814 --> 00:03:21,604
I looked at Lily's window again.

87
00:03:22,094 --> 00:03:24,334
Kept my thumb away from
the button while I did it.

88
00:03:24,354 --> 00:03:25,133
How old?

89
00:03:25,153 --> 00:03:25,813
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Little.

90
00:03:25,833 --> 00:03:26,963
Six, perhaps.

91
00:03:27,333 --> 00:03:28,133
Seven.

92
00:03:28,153 --> 00:03:29,503
It's hard to get much out of her.

93
00:03:29,595 --> 00:03:33,265
I stood on that roof until my
hand went numb around the radio.

94
00:03:33,375 --> 00:03:35,735
Vera never asked about the
window again that night.

95
00:03:35,755 --> 00:03:38,705
She'd found another question
I couldn't walk away from.

96
00:03:39,806 --> 00:03:44,156
Somebody ate my breakfast while
I slept inside a locked store.

97
00:03:44,446 --> 00:03:46,866
I'd put two protein bars beside the tent.

98
00:03:46,886 --> 00:03:51,346
One for when I woke up, one for later,
because apparently I needed a system for

99
00:03:51,366 --> 00:03:53,196
deciding when to eat cardboard.

100
00:03:53,386 --> 00:03:54,496
There was one left.

101
00:03:54,606 --> 00:03:56,136
I checked the sleeping bag.

102
00:03:56,166 --> 00:04:00,176
Turned it inside out. Looked under
the tent and inside both boots.

103
00:04:00,456 --> 00:04:02,906
At the gate, the padlock was closed.

104
00:04:03,236 --> 00:04:04,986
Key thirty-one was still on my belt.

105
00:04:05,236 --> 00:04:06,646
I counted the water twice.

106
00:04:06,916 --> 00:04:08,366
A bottle was missing too.

107
00:04:08,416 --> 00:04:10,666
I could explain losing a protein bar.

108
00:04:10,776 --> 00:04:14,836
I'd spent the night listening to my dead
friend walk past, and my brain was doing

109
00:04:14,856 --> 00:04:16,786
its best to forget the whole thing.

110
00:04:16,976 --> 00:04:17,986
A bottle was harder.

111
00:04:18,250 --> 00:04:20,600
I lined everything up along the back wall.

112
00:04:21,030 --> 00:04:24,820
Bars in one row, cans in
another, water underneath.

113
00:04:25,070 --> 00:04:28,880
Wrote the numbers on a receipt with the
little pencil I used for my shift log.

114
00:04:29,110 --> 00:04:31,620
I hadn't written anything in
that log since the first night.

115
00:04:31,735 --> 00:04:37,465
For a while I sat there trying to
remember the last normal entry.

116
00:04:37,655 --> 00:04:39,285
A door propped open.

117
00:04:39,795 --> 00:04:42,505
A car parked across two spaces.

118
00:04:42,975 --> 00:04:44,685
Something I'd been annoyed about.

119
00:04:44,855 --> 00:04:48,915
Then I heard two pulls on a gate outside,
and I remembered I was supposed to be

120
00:04:48,935 --> 00:04:49,935
counting water.

121
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:55,203
I carried the remaining bars into the
stockroom and put them in a plastic storage

122
00:04:55,223 --> 00:04:56,023
box.

123
00:04:56,043 --> 00:04:58,153
Then I sat beside it until my neck hurt.

124
00:04:58,323 --> 00:04:59,243
Nothing happened.

125
00:04:59,263 --> 00:05:00,733
At nine, I went to the roof.

126
00:05:00,983 --> 00:05:02,193
Three blinks from Lily.

127
00:05:02,363 --> 00:05:03,643
Three back from me.

128
00:05:03,663 --> 00:05:06,853
I kept my body between the
flashlight and the department store.

129
00:05:07,083 --> 00:05:09,033
Vera called as soon as I came downstairs.

130
00:05:09,439 --> 00:05:10,829
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Any luck with supper?

131
00:05:11,131 --> 00:05:12,721
I haven't agreed to anything.

132
00:05:13,032 --> 00:05:14,562
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] You sound tired.

133
00:05:14,957 --> 00:05:16,687
I am tired.

134
00:05:17,213 --> 00:05:18,403
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Get some rest.

135
00:05:18,613 --> 00:05:19,643
We can talk tomorrow.

136
00:05:19,898 --> 00:05:22,768
I stared at the storage
box for another hour.

137
00:05:23,198 --> 00:05:26,148
When I finally slept, I
put it beside my head.

138
00:05:26,278 --> 00:05:28,748
When I woke again, the lid was back on.

139
00:05:28,858 --> 00:05:31,308
One of the catches hadn't
quite clicked shut.

140
00:05:32,098 --> 00:05:33,768
Two more bars were gone.

141
00:05:34,378 --> 00:05:37,788
Whoever was doing this had stood
close enough to watch me sleep.

142
00:05:38,999 --> 00:05:43,309
I put climbing chalk on the floor,
and the footprints went up the wall.

143
00:05:43,419 --> 00:05:46,669
The chalk came in a little white
bag from the climbing display.

144
00:05:46,839 --> 00:05:51,619
I spread it around the food box, under
the stockroom door, and across the narrow

145
00:05:51,639 --> 00:05:53,149
space between the tents.

146
00:05:53,379 --> 00:05:55,349
Then I went back to bed with my boots on.

147
00:05:56,811 --> 00:05:59,121
That was my entire investigation.

148
00:05:59,591 --> 00:06:03,941
Six years in security, and I was
waiting for somebody to step in powder.

149
00:06:04,211 --> 00:06:06,401
I left a fresh bar on top of the box.

150
00:06:06,551 --> 00:06:07,801
The rest went inside it.

151
00:06:07,887 --> 00:06:11,937
I felt ridiculous setting bait with a
breakfast I couldn't afford to lose.

152
00:06:12,027 --> 00:06:14,797
But the gate was the only
way in that I understood.

153
00:06:14,927 --> 00:06:17,807
Whoever had found another way could
bring somebody else through it.

154
00:06:17,827 --> 00:06:19,837
I lay facing the gap between the tents.

155
00:06:20,027 --> 00:06:23,397
If anybody came through
there, this time I'd see them.

156
00:06:23,467 --> 00:06:26,337
Sometime before morning,
I heard plastic bend.

157
00:06:26,530 --> 00:06:30,520
By the time I'd got out of the sleeping
bag, the store was still again.

158
00:06:30,630 --> 00:06:34,880
I left the overhead lights off and
used my flashlight close to the floor.

159
00:06:35,050 --> 00:06:36,080
Small trainers.

160
00:06:36,270 --> 00:06:38,300
A worn patch under the right heel.

161
00:06:38,350 --> 00:06:42,800
The print had a little square of clear floor
in the middle where the sole was split.

162
00:06:43,358 --> 00:06:46,908
The trail came from behind
the climbing wall display.

163
00:06:47,118 --> 00:06:48,488
It went to the food box.

164
00:06:48,678 --> 00:06:49,848
Then it went back.

165
00:06:50,178 --> 00:06:52,028
I moved the display a few inches.

166
00:06:52,458 --> 00:06:55,568
Behind it was a tall storage
rack bolted to the wall.

167
00:06:55,758 --> 00:06:57,888
A shoeprint showed on the bottom shelf.

168
00:06:58,158 --> 00:07:01,108
Another was pressed against
the painted wall halfway up.

169
00:07:01,221 --> 00:07:06,031
Higher still, somebody had wiped
a hand across a dusty pipe.

170
00:07:06,261 --> 00:07:07,971
I followed the pipe with the light.

171
00:07:08,181 --> 00:07:12,451
One ceiling tile was cleaner around
the edges than all the others.

172
00:07:12,581 --> 00:07:14,211
I stood there with my mouth open.

173
00:07:14,361 --> 00:07:15,991
Every door was locked.

174
00:07:16,181 --> 00:07:20,871
Every window was intact. I'd checked the
gates so often that morning my hand hurt.

175
00:07:21,081 --> 00:07:22,931
I hadn't looked up once.

176
00:07:23,258 --> 00:07:26,968
A little white flake dropped
out of the seam above me.

177
00:07:27,098 --> 00:07:28,648
I switched the flashlight off.

178
00:07:28,898 --> 00:07:30,788
Whoever was up there had seen the light.

179
00:07:30,958 --> 00:07:32,308
And they were still there.

180
00:07:33,473 --> 00:07:38,133
I caught the person stealing my food, and
he was wearing shoes held together with

181
00:07:38,153 --> 00:07:38,893
tape.

182
00:07:38,913 --> 00:07:42,263
I waited behind the display
until my bad knee went stiff.

183
00:07:42,473 --> 00:07:44,023
It was barely six in the morning.

184
00:07:44,213 --> 00:07:47,083
Outside, Marcus rattled
the gate and moved on.

185
00:07:47,193 --> 00:07:48,343
The tile lifted.

186
00:07:48,473 --> 00:07:53,953
Two fingers appeared, then a head, then a
very skinny boy lowering himself onto the

187
00:07:53,973 --> 00:07:54,973
top shelf.

188
00:07:55,039 --> 00:07:57,289
He moved carefully.

189
00:07:57,599 --> 00:07:59,729
He knew which bit of the rack squeaked.

190
00:07:59,839 --> 00:08:02,449
He stepped around it before
his foot even touched down.

191
00:08:02,499 --> 00:08:05,189
When he reached the floor,
he went straight to the box.

192
00:08:05,399 --> 00:08:07,119
I waited until he bent over it.

193
00:08:07,139 --> 00:08:09,209
Then I stood up. We looked at each other.

194
00:08:09,259 --> 00:08:11,709
He had a protein bar already in his hand.

195
00:08:11,865 --> 00:08:14,375
The sweatshirt hung past his fingers.

196
00:08:14,565 --> 00:08:19,145
There was a pale clean line around one
wrist where he'd pushed a sleeve up.

197
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:22,235
Everything else about him
looked as dusty as the pipe.

198
00:08:22,305 --> 00:08:25,215
I'd practised this conversation
in my head while I waited.

199
00:08:25,325 --> 00:08:27,895
It had involved a grown
man explaining himself.

200
00:08:28,168 --> 00:08:32,538
I hadn't practised what to do if the thief
looked hungry enough to eat the wrapper.

201
00:08:32,728 --> 00:08:34,298
Put it down, I said.

202
00:08:34,408 --> 00:08:35,288
He put it down.

203
00:08:35,308 --> 00:08:36,878
Then he ran straight at me.

204
00:08:36,973 --> 00:08:42,213
I moved aside because, for a second, that's
what my body thought you did when a kid

205
00:08:42,233 --> 00:08:43,233
ran at you.

206
00:08:43,253 --> 00:08:47,603
He got past, took two steps up the
rack, and nearly reached the pipe.

207
00:08:47,733 --> 00:08:49,343
I caught the back of his sweatshirt.

208
00:08:49,393 --> 00:08:52,083
He twisted so hard the stitching tore.

209
00:08:52,352 --> 00:08:53,352
Let go.

210
00:08:53,930 --> 00:08:55,080
Stop kicking.

211
00:08:55,337 --> 00:08:56,284
Let go.

212
00:08:56,304 --> 00:08:57,224
I did.

213
00:08:57,244 --> 00:09:01,494
He stayed on the second shelf, one
hand on the pipe, watching my hands.

214
00:09:02,124 --> 00:09:04,534
The loose shelf knocked against the wall.

215
00:09:04,644 --> 00:09:07,754
Somewhere outside, a shoe
dragged across the floor.

216
00:09:07,864 --> 00:09:09,034
We both stopped breathing.

217
00:09:09,464 --> 00:09:10,914
A shadow passed the gate.

218
00:09:11,044 --> 00:09:11,924
Paused.

219
00:09:11,944 --> 00:09:12,944
Moved on.

220
00:09:13,244 --> 00:09:15,754
The boy looked toward the
hallway, then back at me.

221
00:09:15,858 --> 00:09:17,408
Don't do that again,

222
00:09:17,694 --> 00:09:18,694
he whispered.

223
00:09:18,994 --> 00:09:23,854
I wanted to tell him I was the adult and
this was my store and he was stealing my

224
00:09:23,874 --> 00:09:24,874
food.

225
00:09:24,954 --> 00:09:26,404
Instead I asked how old he was.

226
00:09:26,589 --> 00:09:27,589
Fifteen.

227
00:09:27,734 --> 00:09:28,701
Your name?

228
00:09:28,721 --> 00:09:29,519
Theo.

229
00:09:29,539 --> 00:09:30,949
Who else is up there?

230
00:09:31,039 --> 00:09:32,729
He tightened his grip on the pipe.

231
00:09:32,943 --> 00:09:33,743
Nobody.

232
00:09:33,763 --> 00:09:35,153
That's why I stay up there.

233
00:09:36,324 --> 00:09:40,924
A fifteen-year-old had been living in
my mall for four months, and I'd never

234
00:09:40,944 --> 00:09:41,844
noticed.

235
00:09:41,864 --> 00:09:44,574
I let him sit on an
overturned camping bucket.

236
00:09:44,684 --> 00:09:46,354
He kept the rack within reach.

237
00:09:46,524 --> 00:09:47,524
Where do you sleep?

238
00:09:47,673 --> 00:09:48,783
Above the cinema.

239
00:09:49,789 --> 00:09:51,159
In the ceiling?

240
00:09:51,496 --> 00:09:53,946
There's a space beside
the projection room.

241
00:09:54,082 --> 00:09:55,292
For four months?

242
00:09:55,562 --> 00:09:56,542
He shrugged.

243
00:09:56,562 --> 00:09:57,752
A tiny movement.

244
00:09:57,882 --> 00:10:00,252
Like he was trying to
make four months smaller.

245
00:10:00,362 --> 00:10:01,472
How did you eat?

246
00:10:01,691 --> 00:10:03,421
People throw stuff out.

247
00:10:03,534 --> 00:10:04,534
And the doors?

248
00:10:04,619 --> 00:10:05,769
I go round them.

249
00:10:05,944 --> 00:10:08,094
I looked up at the tile again.

250
00:10:08,244 --> 00:10:09,654
He pointed toward my belt.

251
00:10:09,882 --> 00:10:11,112
You like checking those.

252
00:10:11,367 --> 00:10:12,657
The keys?

253
00:10:13,451 --> 00:10:14,451
The doors.

254
00:10:14,611 --> 00:10:17,341
You do the same ones twice
when you're on the phone.

255
00:10:17,559 --> 00:10:22,519
I thought about all the nights I'd walked
this building, tugged handles, signed the

256
00:10:22,539 --> 00:10:25,489
log, and told myself everybody was safe.

257
00:10:25,779 --> 00:10:28,599
Theo peeled a strip of
tape away from his trainer.

258
00:10:28,619 --> 00:10:29,829
Pressed it back down.

259
00:10:29,979 --> 00:10:31,749
You sing in the freight elevator,

260
00:10:32,120 --> 00:10:33,100
he said.

261
00:10:33,120 --> 00:10:34,019
I looked at him.

262
00:10:34,039 --> 00:10:35,869
Usually the same song.

263
00:10:36,279 --> 00:10:37,709
You only know some of it.

264
00:10:37,762 --> 00:10:39,212
My face got hot.

265
00:10:39,542 --> 00:10:40,382
Even then.

266
00:10:40,402 --> 00:10:43,172
Even with everything
outside, that still worked.

267
00:10:43,342 --> 00:10:45,172
You can't stay here, I said.

268
00:10:45,982 --> 00:10:50,492
The words came out before I'd
decided what I meant by them.

269
00:10:50,522 --> 00:10:52,372
There were two sentences in my head.

270
00:10:52,442 --> 00:10:53,592
One was about food.

271
00:10:53,682 --> 00:10:57,482
The other was about the man who'd sat outside
my gate and trusted me to know what to

272
00:10:57,502 --> 00:10:57,873
do.

273
00:10:57,893 --> 00:11:00,503
I could hardly look at
that gate in daylight.

274
00:11:00,753 --> 00:11:04,683
Now this kid was sitting six feet from
it, waiting for me to be in charge.

275
00:11:05,053 --> 00:11:06,883
I wanted somebody qualified.

276
00:11:07,273 --> 00:11:08,273
A firefighter.

277
00:11:08,553 --> 00:11:09,553
His dad.

278
00:11:09,613 --> 00:11:11,903
Any adult who'd know
how to keep him alive.

279
00:11:12,273 --> 00:11:14,163
He was looking at the only one available.

280
00:11:14,553 --> 00:11:15,703
Theo stood immediately.

281
00:11:16,009 --> 00:11:17,009
He didn't argue.

282
00:11:17,209 --> 00:11:19,819
Picked up nothing, because
he'd brought nothing.

283
00:11:19,929 --> 00:11:22,339
I heard Marcus at another
gate down the hall.

284
00:11:22,649 --> 00:11:23,679
Theo heard him too.

285
00:11:23,729 --> 00:11:24,879
Wait, I said.

286
00:11:24,949 --> 00:11:26,379
He waited beside the rack.

287
00:11:26,669 --> 00:11:29,799
I reached for a bottle, then
stopped with my hand on it.

288
00:11:29,889 --> 00:11:31,679
Theo watched me count the ones left.

289
00:11:31,889 --> 00:11:33,019
How long have you got?

290
00:11:33,124 --> 00:11:35,254
he asked. About ten days.

291
00:11:35,324 --> 00:11:37,574
Maybe. I was working
it out for one person.

292
00:11:37,744 --> 00:11:39,094
He looked toward the front of the mall.

293
00:11:39,242 --> 00:11:41,552
I know where there's
eight thousand gallons.

294
00:11:42,983 --> 00:11:47,413
The water I needed was
under a hundred dead people.

295
00:11:47,607 --> 00:11:48,607
The fountain,

296
00:11:48,631 --> 00:11:49,631
Theo said.

297
00:11:49,871 --> 00:11:50,871
I stared at him.

298
00:11:50,931 --> 00:11:56,191
In six years I'd taken coins out of that
fountain, fished out a phone, and once

299
00:11:56,211 --> 00:12:00,191
helped a man retrieve an engagement ring
he'd dropped before he got to the important

300
00:12:00,211 --> 00:12:03,501
question. I'd never thought
about where the water came from.

301
00:12:03,702 --> 00:12:04,992
Big tank underneath,

302
00:12:05,334 --> 00:12:06,364
Theo said.

303
00:12:06,564 --> 00:12:08,384
There's a room with all the pumps.

304
00:12:08,404 --> 00:12:10,994
Number's written on the side.

305
00:12:11,185 --> 00:12:12,185
Eight thousand?

306
00:12:12,245 --> 00:12:13,105
He nodded.

307
00:12:13,125 --> 00:12:15,035
I knew the pump-room door.

308
00:12:15,185 --> 00:12:18,295
It opened into the center
court, beside the pretzel place.

309
00:12:18,445 --> 00:12:22,175
On the cameras, that doorway
was buried behind bodies.

310
00:12:22,325 --> 00:12:23,975
The way downstairs is full.

311
00:12:24,165 --> 00:12:25,395
I come from above.

312
00:12:25,688 --> 00:12:28,338
He drew a route in the
chalk with one finger.

313
00:12:29,308 --> 00:12:30,448
Above the cinema.

314
00:12:30,468 --> 00:12:32,158
Across a service walkway.

315
00:12:32,188 --> 00:12:35,758
Down inside the big column beside the
fountain, on a maintenance ladder.

316
00:12:36,028 --> 00:12:38,438
The route ended behind
the locked pump-room door.

317
00:12:38,548 --> 00:12:40,578
I could feel the weight
of the keys on my hip.

318
00:12:40,808 --> 00:12:42,058
Why haven't you gone already?

319
00:12:42,267 --> 00:12:43,857
Nothing to carry it in.

320
00:12:43,989 --> 00:12:48,619
The store around us was full
of camping water containers.

321
00:12:49,169 --> 00:12:51,159
How much can you carry back?

322
00:12:51,329 --> 00:12:51,989
I asked.

323
00:12:52,009 --> 00:12:54,199
He held his hands a little apart.

324
00:12:54,423 --> 00:12:55,453
Small ones.

325
00:12:55,963 --> 00:12:57,273
You have to get them through.

326
00:12:57,575 --> 00:13:02,525
I picked up a container big enough to be
useful, imagined carrying it one-handed

327
00:13:02,615 --> 00:13:04,765
over the court, and put it back.

328
00:13:04,895 --> 00:13:06,765
We settled on two smaller ones.

329
00:13:06,955 --> 00:13:10,485
I tried holding them full,
then lifting them onto a shelf.

330
00:13:10,635 --> 00:13:12,685
My arms shook by the third try.

331
00:13:12,820 --> 00:13:15,550
Theo watched without saying anything.

332
00:13:15,760 --> 00:13:17,150
I wished he'd made a joke.

333
00:13:17,280 --> 00:13:20,580
It would've been easier than watching
him decide whether I could do it.

334
00:13:20,600 --> 00:13:21,620
He looked at them.

335
00:13:21,640 --> 00:13:22,580
Looked at me.

336
00:13:22,600 --> 00:13:24,190
We understood each other then.

337
00:13:24,260 --> 00:13:26,810
I'd been counting bottles
and locking gates.

338
00:13:26,920 --> 00:13:28,870
He'd been counting routes through walls.

339
00:13:29,166 --> 00:13:31,156
That night Vera called again.

340
00:13:31,386 --> 00:13:34,476
She said the little girl
had stopped asking for food.

341
00:13:34,666 --> 00:13:37,956
I held the radio so tightly
the plastic creaked.

342
00:13:38,106 --> 00:13:39,656
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO]
Get some sleep, Danny,

343
00:13:40,019 --> 00:13:40,853
she said.

344
00:13:40,873 --> 00:13:42,403
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] You'll
think better tomorrow.

345
00:13:42,794 --> 00:13:46,704
I sat beside Theo's bucket
after the light went out.

346
00:13:46,774 --> 00:13:48,604
Show me the way, I said.

347
00:13:48,714 --> 00:13:50,004
We bring water back.

348
00:13:50,194 --> 00:13:51,194
You get food.

349
00:13:51,254 --> 00:13:52,704
We work the rest out after.

350
00:13:52,774 --> 00:13:54,844
He looked at the tent, then at the rack.

351
00:13:55,065 --> 00:13:57,635
I'd come down from the
roof a few minutes earlier.

352
00:13:57,865 --> 00:13:58,865
Lily had blinked.

353
00:13:59,025 --> 00:14:00,025
I'd blinked back.

354
00:14:00,045 --> 00:14:03,055
For another night, that was
everything we knew about each other.

355
00:14:03,105 --> 00:14:06,635
My mom had gone into the apartment
with about ten days of insulin.

356
00:14:06,785 --> 00:14:10,855
Every time I counted my water, I
found myself counting her days too.

357
00:14:11,014 --> 00:14:13,884
Getting more water wouldn't
get me across the highway.

358
00:14:14,074 --> 00:14:18,514
But I couldn't do anything for either of
them if I spent the next week getting too

359
00:14:18,534 --> 00:14:20,124
weak to climb the roof ladder.

360
00:14:20,343 --> 00:14:21,343
You coming too?

361
00:14:21,390 --> 00:14:21,990
Yes.

362
00:14:22,010 --> 00:14:23,280
He glanced at my boots.

363
00:14:23,470 --> 00:14:26,380
That was when I started worrying
about what his route could hold.

364
00:14:27,560 --> 00:14:32,830
The first new door I opened
was beside a kid's bed.

365
00:14:33,140 --> 00:14:35,030
We left before the mall got bright.

366
00:14:35,240 --> 00:14:39,460
I took empty camping containers, a
flashlight, and a strap from the climbing

367
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,340
display.

368
00:14:40,360 --> 00:14:42,430
I took the battery out of Marcus's radio.

369
00:14:42,480 --> 00:14:45,490
Wrapped the keyring in a sock
so the metal would stay quiet.

370
00:14:45,762 --> 00:14:49,292
Theo made me try the rack
without the containers first.

371
00:14:49,462 --> 00:14:52,492
On the second shelf I reached
for something that looked solid.

372
00:14:52,622 --> 00:14:54,992
He caught my hand before
I put any weight on it.

373
00:14:55,067 --> 00:14:57,017
That's for holding the ceiling up,

374
00:14:57,201 --> 00:14:58,201
he said.

375
00:14:58,237 --> 00:14:59,467
It won't hold you.

376
00:14:59,615 --> 00:15:03,545
He moved my hand to a
thick support above it.

377
00:15:03,735 --> 00:15:06,315
I nodded as if I'd
understood that all along.

378
00:15:06,335 --> 00:15:09,225
Then I climbed down and started again.

379
00:15:09,615 --> 00:15:11,165
Theo watched all of it.

380
00:15:11,303 --> 00:15:12,723
You always carry that many?

381
00:15:12,925 --> 00:15:14,195
Every night.

382
00:15:14,274 --> 00:15:15,404
Must've been annoying.

383
00:15:15,710 --> 00:15:16,710
It had been.

384
00:15:16,930 --> 00:15:21,570
I would've given almost anything to be
annoyed by that sound again on an ordinary

385
00:15:21,590 --> 00:15:22,590
Tuesday.

386
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:27,930
Above the store, the air was warm and
smelled like dust from a heater somebody had

387
00:15:27,950 --> 00:15:29,060
just switched on.

388
00:15:29,230 --> 00:15:31,420
Theo showed me where
the metal supports ran.

389
00:15:31,584 --> 00:15:34,004
I followed them on my hands and knees.

390
00:15:34,024 --> 00:15:36,504
Kept my weight on the heavy steel.

391
00:15:36,524 --> 00:15:40,414
The ceiling tiles shifted below
us when I breathed too hard.

392
00:15:40,864 --> 00:15:44,034
Over the cinema, he stopped
beside a stained blanket.

393
00:15:44,244 --> 00:15:49,844
There were three empty water bottles, a
folded hoodie, and a photograph turned face

394
00:15:49,864 --> 00:15:50,604
down.

395
00:15:50,624 --> 00:15:53,334
He slid that underneath the
blanket before I could see it.

396
00:15:53,452 --> 00:15:59,102
A door beside the little platform had
CINEMA SERVICE stencilled across it.

397
00:15:59,252 --> 00:16:00,322
Key seventeen fit.

398
00:16:00,532 --> 00:16:02,962
Theo watched the lock turn
as though I'd done a trick.

399
00:16:03,192 --> 00:16:04,662
You've been climbing around this?

400
00:16:04,844 --> 00:16:05,844
For a while.

401
00:16:06,019 --> 00:16:09,069
I opened it just wide enough
for us to get through.

402
00:16:09,299 --> 00:16:12,769
On the other side was the service
walkway over the center court.

403
00:16:13,039 --> 00:16:16,089
Through gaps beneath the rail,
I could see the tops of heads.

404
00:16:16,539 --> 00:16:17,649
Theo stepped out first.

405
00:16:17,859 --> 00:16:20,409
Halfway across, the proper walkway ended.

406
00:16:20,519 --> 00:16:24,409
Beyond it, the route followed a pair of
supports above the suspended ceiling.

407
00:16:24,599 --> 00:16:25,573
I stopped.

408
00:16:25,593 --> 00:16:26,803
Theo looked back.

409
00:16:27,040 --> 00:16:30,110
Don't put your foot where
you think the floor is.

410
00:16:31,284 --> 00:16:35,694
My best friend walked his rounds
while I crawled over his head.

411
00:16:36,384 --> 00:16:38,054
Theo crossed the first gap easily.

412
00:16:38,284 --> 00:16:41,954
I watched where his hands went, then
tried to put mine in the same places.

413
00:16:42,544 --> 00:16:46,664
There was a difference between watching a
skinny fifteen-year-old do something and

414
00:16:46,684 --> 00:16:48,814
asking my knees to do it afterward.

415
00:16:49,127 --> 00:16:50,957
Sweat ran down my nose.

416
00:16:51,147 --> 00:16:53,557
I caught it on my sleeve
before it could fall.

417
00:16:53,767 --> 00:16:56,497
One of the emergency lights
flickered underneath us.

418
00:16:56,527 --> 00:17:00,417
For a second the shadows moved and
I tightened both hands on the steel.

419
00:17:00,707 --> 00:17:03,017
Theo stopped with me. He
didn't tell me to hurry.

420
00:17:03,151 --> 00:17:04,151
Next hand,

421
00:17:04,268 --> 00:17:05,268
he whispered.

422
00:17:05,288 --> 00:17:06,161
I moved it.

423
00:17:06,181 --> 00:17:07,311
Now your knee.

424
00:17:07,509 --> 00:17:08,759
I moved that too.

425
00:17:08,969 --> 00:17:12,199
After a while I could do two
movements without being told.

426
00:17:12,389 --> 00:17:13,989
I was grateful he didn't mention it.

427
00:17:14,009 --> 00:17:15,959
Below us, the fountain was dark.

428
00:17:16,289 --> 00:17:17,439
Coins lay on the bottom.

429
00:17:17,589 --> 00:17:21,329
The people around it were standing
shoulder to shoulder in places, their faces

430
00:17:21,349 --> 00:17:23,359
turned toward the food-court doors.

431
00:17:23,489 --> 00:17:24,979
I stopped counting at a hundred.

432
00:17:25,123 --> 00:17:27,233
Theo reached back for a container.

433
00:17:27,523 --> 00:17:28,673
I passed it forward.

434
00:17:28,783 --> 00:17:32,133
He put it on a solid section,
then came back for the other one.

435
00:17:32,303 --> 00:17:33,023
Slow.

436
00:17:33,043 --> 00:17:34,653
Everything had to be slow.

437
00:17:34,743 --> 00:17:36,833
A gate rattled at the far end of the hall.

438
00:17:36,923 --> 00:17:38,953
I knew who it was before I saw him.

439
00:17:39,012 --> 00:17:42,332
Marcus came around the corner
and stopped at the first store.

440
00:17:42,472 --> 00:17:43,712
Two pulls on the gate.

441
00:17:43,732 --> 00:17:44,612
A pause.

442
00:17:44,632 --> 00:17:45,632
Then the next one.

443
00:17:45,692 --> 00:17:47,702
I found myself waiting for him to look up.

444
00:17:48,032 --> 00:17:49,182
Theo touched my shoulder.

445
00:17:49,312 --> 00:17:51,002
I moved my knee to give him room.

446
00:17:51,092 --> 00:17:52,762
The bit of metal under it folded.

447
00:17:53,002 --> 00:17:57,032
I dropped far enough that my
stomach hit the edge of the support.

448
00:17:57,182 --> 00:17:59,112
My right leg punched through a tile.

449
00:17:59,342 --> 00:18:02,052
Something caught the leather
of my boot and held it there.

450
00:18:02,162 --> 00:18:03,692
Pieces fell into the court.

451
00:18:03,742 --> 00:18:05,692
The first one struck the fountain's rim.

452
00:18:05,822 --> 00:18:07,392
A head turned. Then another.

453
00:18:07,628 --> 00:18:09,018
Theo caught my wrist.

454
00:18:09,328 --> 00:18:13,378
I tried to pull my knee back, and
a sharp edge dug into my thigh.

455
00:18:13,548 --> 00:18:15,438
Below, Marcus stopped walking.

456
00:18:15,548 --> 00:18:17,578
He lifted his face toward my foot.

457
00:18:17,708 --> 00:18:19,818
My boot began to slide off.

458
00:18:21,031 --> 00:18:25,221
The kid I'd told to leave was the only
thing keeping me out of that crowd.

459
00:18:25,571 --> 00:18:28,341
Theo lay flat and reached
for my other wrist.

460
00:18:28,491 --> 00:18:30,441
His fingers slipped on my sleeve.

461
00:18:30,681 --> 00:18:31,691
Give me your hand.

462
00:18:31,910 --> 00:18:33,360
I tried.

463
00:18:33,950 --> 00:18:38,040
A long piece of the tile broke
away and hit someone's shoulder.

464
00:18:38,830 --> 00:18:40,880
People began pushing under the hole.

465
00:18:41,970 --> 00:18:44,580
Slowly, one body leaning into the next.

466
00:18:44,970 --> 00:18:47,140
Marcus stood among them, looking up.

467
00:18:47,281 --> 00:18:49,611
I could see the worn patch on his cap.

468
00:18:49,781 --> 00:18:54,181
I'd stood beside him in the office while
he picked at it with his thumbnail and told

469
00:18:54,201 --> 00:18:55,931
me a joke I'd already heard.

470
00:18:56,041 --> 00:18:57,311
I nearly said his name.

471
00:18:57,581 --> 00:18:58,751
Theo hit my arm.

472
00:18:58,901 --> 00:18:59,709
Look at me.

473
00:18:59,729 --> 00:19:00,729
I looked up.

474
00:19:00,749 --> 00:19:02,799
He was reaching for the strap I'd brought.

475
00:19:02,889 --> 00:19:07,539
Getting it around the heavy support with
one hand while the other held my sleeve.

476
00:19:07,861 --> 00:19:09,351
You have to let go,

477
00:19:09,652 --> 00:19:10,652
he whispered.

478
00:19:11,012 --> 00:19:12,262
I shook my head.

479
00:19:12,466 --> 00:19:13,466
One hand.

480
00:19:13,626 --> 00:19:14,626
I need the strap.

481
00:19:14,678 --> 00:19:18,248
His sleeve was bunched in my fist.

482
00:19:19,078 --> 00:19:22,348
I'd been holding him so hard the
cloth had twisted around his arm.

483
00:19:22,918 --> 00:19:24,548
I made myself open my fingers.

484
00:19:24,718 --> 00:19:27,718
He fed the strap around the support
and leaned his weight into it.

485
00:19:27,738 --> 00:19:29,618
I heard fabric pull tight.

486
00:19:29,638 --> 00:19:32,898
His shoe slipped against the brace, and
he caught himself with a sharp little

487
00:19:32,918 --> 00:19:33,620
breath.

488
00:19:33,640 --> 00:19:36,670
Then his hand was back
in front of my face.

489
00:19:36,900 --> 00:19:37,900
Elbow up,

490
00:19:38,195 --> 00:19:39,190
he said.

491
00:19:39,210 --> 00:19:40,220
You have to help.

492
00:19:40,445 --> 00:19:43,115
I got an elbow onto the steel.

493
00:19:43,325 --> 00:19:46,595
Pushed until my shoulder felt
as though it was coming apart.

494
00:19:46,945 --> 00:19:49,595
Theo leaned back against
the strap and pulled.

495
00:19:49,925 --> 00:19:51,535
My boot stayed where it was.

496
00:19:51,685 --> 00:19:53,135
My foot came out of it.

497
00:19:53,185 --> 00:19:55,435
For a second I thought
that meant I was falling.

498
00:19:55,723 --> 00:20:01,243
Then my knee slid over the edge, and Theo
dragged me onto the solid platform with

499
00:20:01,263 --> 00:20:01,683
him.

500
00:20:01,703 --> 00:20:04,473
We lay there together,
breathing into our sleeves.

501
00:20:04,723 --> 00:20:07,613
Below us, the boot finally came loose.

502
00:20:07,863 --> 00:20:11,633
It landed inside the empty fountain with
a noise that seemed to go on forever.

503
00:20:11,923 --> 00:20:14,793
Theo pressed both palms
against the metal and waited.

504
00:20:15,019 --> 00:20:17,909
Eventually the pushing slowed.

505
00:20:18,339 --> 00:20:19,949
A few faces turned away.

506
00:20:20,099 --> 00:20:21,099
I looked at him.

507
00:20:21,119 --> 00:20:23,669
His trouser leg was torn at the calf.

508
00:20:23,859 --> 00:20:28,089
There was blood on the sharp brace
he'd crawled across to reach me.

509
00:20:28,119 --> 00:20:29,889
He pulled the fabric down over it.

510
00:20:30,018 --> 00:20:32,188
You can walk without that shoe,

511
00:20:32,398 --> 00:20:33,398
he whispered.

512
00:20:33,498 --> 00:20:37,288
Somewhere ahead and
below us, water dripped.

513
00:20:38,407 --> 00:20:43,567
We found enough water to keep the whole
mall alive, and Theo told me what had

514
00:20:43,587 --> 00:20:44,757
brought the dead there.

515
00:20:45,067 --> 00:20:48,037
The maintenance ladder ran
down inside the service column.

516
00:20:48,147 --> 00:20:52,057
At the bottom, a narrow hatch opened
into the pump room beneath the fountain.

517
00:20:52,288 --> 00:20:55,378
I put my good foot on each rung first.

518
00:20:55,648 --> 00:20:59,358
Theo stayed close enough to hear every
breath I was trying to keep quiet.

519
00:20:59,508 --> 00:21:01,028
The tank took up most of the room.

520
00:21:01,048 --> 00:21:05,898
EIGHT THOUSAND GALLONS was printed on
a plate beside its inspection window.

521
00:21:06,208 --> 00:21:07,698
There was water behind the glass.

522
00:21:07,918 --> 00:21:12,068
I put my hand against the tank
and left it there for a while.

523
00:21:12,218 --> 00:21:15,688
We still had to get it back and
treat it with the gear in the store.

524
00:21:16,238 --> 00:21:19,888
But I could stop staring at the last
few bottles every time I swallowed.

525
00:21:20,538 --> 00:21:23,108
Theo eased himself onto the bottom rung.

526
00:21:23,158 --> 00:21:24,588
He was favouring his leg.

527
00:21:24,838 --> 00:21:25,838
You hurt?

528
00:21:25,865 --> 00:21:26,639
Caught it.

529
00:21:26,659 --> 00:21:27,659
I saw.

530
00:21:27,735 --> 00:21:28,885
Then why'd you ask?

531
00:21:29,084 --> 00:21:30,374
I nearly smiled.

532
00:21:30,664 --> 00:21:32,414
We filled what we could carry.

533
00:21:32,924 --> 00:21:36,654
The handles pulled at my fingers
when I lifted the containers.

534
00:21:37,244 --> 00:21:39,914
We'd be drinking what we
carried back for days.

535
00:21:40,344 --> 00:21:42,854
After that, we'd have to come again.

536
00:21:43,084 --> 00:21:46,054
The thought of that crossing
again made me put one down.

537
00:21:46,584 --> 00:21:47,560
Theo noticed.

538
00:21:47,580 --> 00:21:49,830
We can find a better bit to cross,

539
00:21:50,192 --> 00:21:51,192
he said.

540
00:21:51,572 --> 00:21:52,602
You know one?

541
00:21:52,795 --> 00:21:53,795
I can look.

542
00:21:54,012 --> 00:21:55,562
I held the handle again.

543
00:21:55,732 --> 00:21:59,702
He'd spent four months figuring
this place out because he had to.

544
00:22:00,172 --> 00:22:02,122
I was going to have to
start doing the same.

545
00:22:02,632 --> 00:22:06,502
Outside the pump-room door, a
shoe scraped along the floor.

546
00:22:06,652 --> 00:22:08,382
Dust shook out of the frame.

547
00:22:08,632 --> 00:22:10,262
Theo stared at that door.

548
00:22:10,429 --> 00:22:11,719
This is where they were,

549
00:22:11,957 --> 00:22:12,817
he said.

550
00:22:12,837 --> 00:22:13,722
Who?

551
00:22:13,742 --> 00:22:14,772
The drill people.

552
00:22:15,103 --> 00:22:17,033
I set the container down.

553
00:22:17,170 --> 00:22:18,170
Three of them.

554
00:22:18,230 --> 00:22:19,900
A woman and two men.

555
00:22:20,030 --> 00:22:21,420
Behind the pretzel place.

556
00:22:21,690 --> 00:22:22,510
First night.

557
00:22:22,530 --> 00:22:23,760
What time?

558
00:22:24,051 --> 00:22:25,051
One-thirty.

559
00:22:25,151 --> 00:22:27,181
I could see the clock through the opening.

560
00:22:27,355 --> 00:22:28,355
One-thirty.

561
00:22:28,415 --> 00:22:31,645
Ten minutes before Marcus called
about the man on the ramp.

562
00:22:31,804 --> 00:22:33,354
They were cutting through the wall,

563
00:22:33,514 --> 00:22:34,514
Theo said.

564
00:22:34,617 --> 00:22:36,307
Loud as a chainsaw.

565
00:22:36,497 --> 00:22:38,447
I could hear it all the way at the cinema.

566
00:22:38,700 --> 00:22:40,730
He rubbed his sleeve over his nose.

567
00:22:41,036 --> 00:22:44,086
People started coming in.
Through the service hall.

568
00:22:44,196 --> 00:22:45,306
They just kept coming.

569
00:22:45,550 --> 00:22:47,380
What did the woman do?

570
00:22:47,614 --> 00:22:48,984
Told them to keep drilling.

571
00:22:50,228 --> 00:22:55,768
The dead had followed a drill into my
mall, and my best friend had been in their

572
00:22:55,788 --> 00:22:56,328
way.

573
00:22:56,348 --> 00:22:58,938
I sat on the bottom rung beside Theo.

574
00:22:59,008 --> 00:23:02,828
Through the door, I could hear
somebody's hand dragging over the wall.

575
00:23:02,848 --> 00:23:04,198
The woman on my radio?

576
00:23:04,228 --> 00:23:05,053
I asked.

577
00:23:05,073 --> 00:23:06,073
Same voice.

578
00:23:06,473 --> 00:23:08,483
I heard her in your store last night.

579
00:23:09,253 --> 00:23:10,253
You're sure?

580
00:23:10,405 --> 00:23:12,995
She was right below me when
they were drilling, Danny.

581
00:23:13,490 --> 00:23:14,660
I looked at the door.

582
00:23:14,870 --> 00:23:15,810
They saw them?

583
00:23:15,830 --> 00:23:16,830
Theo nodded.

584
00:23:16,859 --> 00:23:18,329
One of the men went to look.

585
00:23:18,399 --> 00:23:19,449
Came back running.

586
00:23:19,619 --> 00:23:21,349
The woman kept saying another minute.

587
00:23:21,479 --> 00:23:22,929
And then?

588
00:23:22,982 --> 00:23:25,932
They took the machine and
went through the staff door.

589
00:23:26,142 --> 00:23:28,312
I stayed where I was until it got quiet.

590
00:23:28,492 --> 00:23:29,882
The food court.

591
00:23:30,232 --> 00:23:31,262
The broken glass.

592
00:23:31,732 --> 00:23:33,402
The service halls filling up.

593
00:23:33,572 --> 00:23:37,432
I'd watched all those cameras and thought
the crowd was wandering through any door

594
00:23:37,452 --> 00:23:38,452
it found.

595
00:23:38,812 --> 00:23:40,322
I'd been watching where they went.

596
00:23:40,632 --> 00:23:42,362
Theo had heard what they were following.

597
00:23:42,472 --> 00:23:43,742
Was there a kid with them?

598
00:23:43,832 --> 00:23:45,962
Theo shook his head. A little girl?

599
00:23:46,126 --> 00:23:46,785
No.

600
00:23:46,805 --> 00:23:48,715
I heard Vera's voice again.

601
00:23:48,765 --> 00:23:50,215
Soft through the speaker.

602
00:23:50,305 --> 00:23:52,595
The little girl had
stopped asking for food.

603
00:23:52,705 --> 00:23:55,695
I stood up too fast and hit
my shoulder on the ladder.

604
00:23:55,845 --> 00:23:58,335
Theo caught the container
before it struck the floor.

605
00:23:58,500 --> 00:24:02,150
For a moment I wanted to go
straight to the department store.

606
00:24:02,400 --> 00:24:06,750
Stand outside her gate and make her
tell me why she'd kept that drill going.

607
00:24:07,280 --> 00:24:09,250
My keys were still wrapped in the sock.

608
00:24:09,500 --> 00:24:13,090
I closed my hand around them until
the teeth pressed through the fabric.

609
00:24:13,268 --> 00:24:14,094
Danny,

610
00:24:14,114 --> 00:24:15,114
Theo said.

611
00:24:15,254 --> 00:24:16,234
I looked at his leg.

612
00:24:16,254 --> 00:24:18,744
At the blood drying on
the edge of his trainer.

613
00:24:18,794 --> 00:24:20,144
He had followed me down here.

614
00:24:20,174 --> 00:24:22,044
Now he was waiting for me to get him back.

615
00:24:22,114 --> 00:24:23,114
I picked up the water.

616
00:24:23,194 --> 00:24:25,574
On the return trip, we moved
around the broken section.

617
00:24:25,594 --> 00:24:27,184
It took nearly an hour.

618
00:24:27,294 --> 00:24:29,364
I could see my boot in the fountain below.

619
00:24:29,463 --> 00:24:31,093
I could see Marcus too.

620
00:24:31,443 --> 00:24:34,113
At the cinema, Theo stopped
to pick up his blanket.

621
00:24:34,183 --> 00:24:36,423
He tucked the photograph inside it.

622
00:24:36,443 --> 00:24:38,793
I pretended to be busy
with the containers.

623
00:24:39,083 --> 00:24:42,933
I got back to Summit Outdoors
in one boot and a filthy sock.

624
00:24:43,023 --> 00:24:46,033
Theo went down first and cleared
a place for the containers.

625
00:24:46,283 --> 00:24:48,233
Then he steadied the rack while I climbed.

626
00:24:48,407 --> 00:24:51,597
I reached the floor and
put my hand on the padlock.

627
00:24:51,987 --> 00:24:52,907
Closed.

628
00:24:52,927 --> 00:24:54,097
Exactly where I'd left it.

629
00:24:54,347 --> 00:24:56,357
I let go and turned toward Theo.

630
00:24:56,547 --> 00:25:00,467
He was sitting on the bucket, trying to
bend his trouser leg far enough to see the

631
00:25:00,487 --> 00:25:03,597
cut. I'd checked that lock so many times.

632
00:25:04,167 --> 00:25:07,457
Theo had just brought me home
without going anywhere near it.

633
00:25:07,565 --> 00:25:09,235
I got the first-aid box.

634
00:25:09,605 --> 00:25:12,015
At nine, I climbed to the roof alone.

635
00:25:12,465 --> 00:25:13,595
Three lights from Lily.

636
00:25:13,825 --> 00:25:14,825
Three back.

637
00:25:15,205 --> 00:25:19,165
I held the roof hatch open a little on the
way down, so I could see whether Theo was

638
00:25:19,185 --> 00:25:20,185
still there.

639
00:25:20,285 --> 00:25:21,855
He was asleep beside the water.

640
00:25:23,105 --> 00:25:27,595
I told the boy who'd saved me to pick a
tent, and he asked what it would cost.

641
00:25:27,745 --> 00:25:29,655
We'd got back the afternoon before.

642
00:25:29,825 --> 00:25:33,765
I'd used bottled water to clean the scrape
on his leg and found a bandage in the

643
00:25:33,785 --> 00:25:34,855
first-aid display.

644
00:25:34,925 --> 00:25:37,215
He'd let me do it without
looking at me once.

645
00:25:37,496 --> 00:25:39,646
I'd asked him to tell me if it got worse.

646
00:25:40,276 --> 00:25:42,966
He'd said he would, much too quickly.

647
00:25:43,176 --> 00:25:48,156
Later, I'd found him putting the empty
wrapper from his bandage inside another

648
00:25:48,176 --> 00:25:52,906
wrapper, folding both down until
they took up almost no room.

649
00:25:53,116 --> 00:25:54,586
He'd done the same with his food.

650
00:25:54,869 --> 00:25:56,099
I knew that habit.

651
00:25:56,329 --> 00:25:58,579
I'd seen it in the
places above the cinema.

652
00:25:58,769 --> 00:26:03,119
A whole life packed small enough that you
could move it before somebody told you to.

653
00:26:03,189 --> 00:26:06,939
That morning he was beside the rack
with his blanket rolled under one arm.

654
00:26:06,989 --> 00:26:07,783
Where are you going?

655
00:26:07,803 --> 00:26:08,763
Back.

656
00:26:08,783 --> 00:26:10,713
Your leg's hurting.

657
00:26:10,957 --> 00:26:11,957
It's fine.

658
00:26:12,178 --> 00:26:14,368
He shifted his weight onto the other foot.

659
00:26:14,738 --> 00:26:16,088
I looked at the ceiling tile.

660
00:26:16,258 --> 00:26:20,668
His way out was three shelves up,
above the pipe he'd used while I slept.

661
00:26:21,178 --> 00:26:22,788
Pick a tent, I said.

662
00:26:22,898 --> 00:26:23,898
He watched me.

663
00:26:24,018 --> 00:26:25,018
Any of them.

664
00:26:25,098 --> 00:26:26,188
Except that one.

665
00:26:26,318 --> 00:26:27,328
I'm in that one.

666
00:26:27,381 --> 00:26:28,381
For how long?

667
00:26:28,554 --> 00:26:29,824
We'll work it out.

668
00:26:30,013 --> 00:26:31,013
What do you want?

669
00:26:31,185 --> 00:26:34,755
That question made me put
down the box I was holding.

670
00:26:35,045 --> 00:26:36,055
Help with the water.

671
00:26:36,225 --> 00:26:37,395
Keep things quiet.

672
00:26:37,565 --> 00:26:39,385
Tell me if you hear people up there.

673
00:26:39,405 --> 00:26:40,385
He waited.

674
00:26:40,405 --> 00:26:41,975
That's it, I said.

675
00:26:42,085 --> 00:26:44,335
I got him a clean sweatshirt from a shelf.

676
00:26:44,465 --> 00:26:48,765
He folded it so carefully before he put it
down that I had to find something else to

677
00:26:48,785 --> 00:26:49,570
look at.

678
00:26:49,590 --> 00:26:51,560
Vera called near dusk.

679
00:26:51,804 --> 00:26:52,544
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Danny.

680
00:26:52,564 --> 00:26:53,954
Any room at the inn?

681
00:26:54,134 --> 00:26:56,424
I held the radio close to my ear.

682
00:26:56,582 --> 00:26:57,520
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Still there?

683
00:26:57,540 --> 00:26:58,540
she asked.

684
00:26:58,660 --> 00:26:59,870
I pressed the button.

685
00:27:00,060 --> 00:27:01,870
You said you were trying on a coat.

686
00:27:01,988 --> 00:27:02,988
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Yes.

687
00:27:04,031 --> 00:27:05,561
Before the mall closed.

688
00:27:05,753 --> 00:27:10,923
[WOMAN ON THE RADIO] Eventually you're going to
have to explain this interest in my shopping.

689
00:27:11,213 --> 00:27:13,823
Theo was watching me from the open tent.

690
00:27:13,973 --> 00:27:15,183
I let go of the button.

691
00:27:15,293 --> 00:27:16,643
Left her waiting this time.

692
00:27:16,673 --> 00:27:19,303
At five to nine, I took the
flashlight from the shelf.

693
00:27:19,513 --> 00:27:21,423
Theo pulled on the clean sweatshirt.

694
00:27:21,508 --> 00:27:22,457
Can I see?

695
00:27:22,477 --> 00:27:23,477
he asked.

696
00:27:24,504 --> 00:27:29,014
A stranger blinked my daughter's goodnight
signal from the department store roof.

697
00:27:29,244 --> 00:27:32,084
Before that happened, I
let Theo come up with me.

698
00:27:32,104 --> 00:27:36,254
He stood a little behind the hatch,
keeping his weight off the bandaged leg.

699
00:27:36,324 --> 00:27:40,414
Across the highway, Parkview was
barely visible against the sky.

700
00:27:40,524 --> 00:27:41,854
I found the tenth floor.

701
00:27:41,944 --> 00:27:44,034
Counted to the fourth
window from the left.

702
00:27:44,218 --> 00:27:45,788
I always counted.

703
00:27:46,418 --> 00:27:48,068
Even when I already knew where to look.

704
00:27:48,138 --> 00:27:50,308
At nine, the flashlight came on.

705
00:27:50,438 --> 00:27:50,898
One.

706
00:27:50,918 --> 00:27:51,968
Two. Three.

707
00:27:52,078 --> 00:27:53,408
I answered with my own.

708
00:27:53,498 --> 00:27:56,068
My hands were steadier than
they'd been the night before.

709
00:27:56,138 --> 00:27:57,468
I had water downstairs.

710
00:27:57,738 --> 00:28:02,298
There was another person waiting beside me,
alive, who could hear something fall and

711
00:28:02,318 --> 00:28:03,318
help me pick it up.

712
00:28:03,409 --> 00:28:08,759
It took so little to make me feel better
that I almost missed the light to my right.

713
00:28:09,049 --> 00:28:11,299
It came from the department store roof.

714
00:28:11,529 --> 00:28:11,989
One.

715
00:28:12,009 --> 00:28:12,589
Two.

716
00:28:12,609 --> 00:28:13,329
Three.

717
00:28:13,349 --> 00:28:15,919
Pointed across the
highway. Toward her window.

718
00:28:17,029 --> 00:28:18,259
I lowered my flashlight.

719
00:28:18,469 --> 00:28:19,879
I wanted to blink again.

720
00:28:20,089 --> 00:28:21,239
Correct it somehow.

721
00:28:21,369 --> 00:28:23,379
Tell Lily which light was mine.

722
00:28:23,566 --> 00:28:27,476
But we had three flashes, and
we had the emergency signal.

723
00:28:27,546 --> 00:28:28,406
That was all.

724
00:28:28,426 --> 00:28:31,216
I'd never taught her what to
do when somebody else answered.

725
00:28:31,306 --> 00:28:35,336
My thumb rested on the switch while
the department store roof went dark.

726
00:28:35,406 --> 00:28:38,136
I kept it there until I was
sure I wouldn't press it.

727
00:28:38,366 --> 00:28:40,136
Theo looked from that roof to me.

728
00:28:40,223 --> 00:28:41,223
Who is that?

729
00:28:41,248 --> 00:28:42,248
he asked.

730
00:28:43,068 --> 00:28:45,598
I put the light in my
pocket before I answered.

731
00:28:46,628 --> 00:28:47,628
The woman.

732
00:28:48,728 --> 00:28:50,558
The radio stayed off.

733
00:28:51,848 --> 00:28:55,358
In front of us, Lily's window went dark.

734
00:28:56,688 --> 00:28:58,298
Our goodnight was over.

735
00:28:59,548 --> 00:29:01,118
Somebody else had joined it.

736
00:29:02,448 --> 00:29:05,118
I stood there until
Theo touched my sleeve.

737
00:29:05,459 --> 00:29:06,909
He was looking at the keys.

738
00:29:07,379 --> 00:29:10,189
The sock had come loose when
I'd put the flashlight away.

739
00:29:10,299 --> 00:29:13,109
The last red tag hung against my hand.

740
00:29:13,230 --> 00:29:14,440
What's B3?

741
00:29:14,704 --> 00:29:15,664
he asked.

742
00:29:15,684 --> 00:29:16,684
I looked down.

743
00:29:16,984 --> 00:29:17,574
Why?

744
00:29:17,594 --> 00:29:18,554
That woman.

745
00:29:18,574 --> 00:29:21,304
She kept saying it. Down to B3.

746
00:29:21,454 --> 00:29:22,454
Get to the door.

747
00:29:22,597 --> 00:29:25,327
I closed my fingers around the tag.

748
00:29:25,694 --> 00:29:27,784
They weren't trying to get into a shop,

749
00:29:28,054 --> 00:29:29,054
he said.

750
00:29:29,151 --> 00:29:31,121
They were trying to get underneath it.

751
00:29:31,316 --> 00:29:34,626
I thought of Walt tapping the last key.

752
00:29:35,196 --> 00:29:36,196
Don't ask.

753
00:29:36,416 --> 00:29:38,066
Across the highway was my daughter.

754
00:29:38,416 --> 00:29:41,326
Across the roof was a
woman copying her signal.

755
00:29:41,736 --> 00:29:44,786
And the thing that woman wanted
was hanging from my belt.

756
00:29:45,236 --> 00:29:47,366
What did she think was behind that door?
